## **Conclusion**

This project provided valuable insights into the relationship between founding team composition and startup funding outcomes. While conventional wisdom about two-founder teams was confirmed descriptively, the analysis revealed that funding stage is a far stronger predictor of investment amount than founder count alone.

The findings emphasize the complexity of startup success, where team composition is just one of many factors. Future research incorporating founder experience, market dynamics, and longitudinal tracking could provide even richer understanding of what drives startup outcomes.

From a personal learning perspective, this project enhanced my skills in data cleaning, exploratory analysis, statistical reasoning, and communicating insights—all critical competencies for a data scientist working at the intersection of business and technology.

